<http://data.silknow.org/object/99ff9c8a-645d-3adb-a704-3f537eadaca2>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "Nuance in Nature" , "Herons, shown standing in stylized water, were introduced into the Japanese design repertory during the Muromachi period (1338-1573), along with other birds that were at first considered novelties, such as cormorants, swallows, and sparrows. \nThe stylized linear composition of the water illustrates the traditional Japanese treatment of rivers and ponds, as well as the popular motif of a sandbar. Originally, water imagery was included to convey its power to refresh and enrich." , "February 16 - July 8, 2007" ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/4fad5de2-b903-3347-a6e5-4c2190788e82> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    "Exhibition" ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "February 16 - July 8, 2007" , "Nuance in Nature" , "Herons, shown standing in stylized water, were introduced into the Japanese design repertory during the Muromachi period (1338-1573), along with other birds that were at first considered novelties, such as cormorants, swallows, and sparrows. \nThe stylized linear composition of the water illustrates the traditional Japanese treatment of rivers and ponds, as well as the popular motif of a sandbar. Originally, water imagery was included to convey its power to refresh and enrich." ;
        schema:contentUrl   <https://risdmuseum.org/exhibitions-events/exhibitions/nuance-nature> .

